00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:29.025
I'm talking about Dr. Phil
everybody, check this out.

00:00:29.025 --> 00:00:31.608
(upbeat music)

00:00:52.028 --> 00:00:53.443
Hey!
- Hey!

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.703
What's up?
- What?

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.110
So be honest with me.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.300
This is the weirdest
place you've ever met up

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.920
for a therapy session.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.110
- This isn't a therapy session, right?

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.940
'Cause this would be in
the running right here.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.380
- Oh no, of course not.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.750
There's no, I don't need therapy
right now at all, Dr. Phil.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.830
No, everything's great.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.990
Everything's lining up just perfectly.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.896
- Not a weird year.
- No.

00:01:22.896 --> 00:01:23.729
- Nothing going on?
- This had been a

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:24.890
such a, it's such a,

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.180
you know what, I feel light I've yeah.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.120
- Yeah, I have to say
you look very at home

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.480
in that big old truck.
- This is,

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.840
Hey, this is my truck
for like 15 years now.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.610
This, his name is sunny.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:36.443
- I would have to say,

00:01:36.443 --> 00:01:37.276
you look very at home in that truck.

00:01:37.276 --> 00:01:39.080
- Thank, and you look very at home.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.910
What kind of wheels are those?

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.130
- This is a 57 Chevy.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:44.723
- Oh my gosh, it's beautiful.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.180
- Did you name your car?

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.150
- The Beast.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.673
- Did you just name it?
- No.

00:01:53.673 --> 00:01:55.340
(laughter)

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.060
- The beast?
- The beast.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.210
- The beast, I like it.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.240
- This was my dream car
when I was growing up,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.500
but there was no way I could afford it.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.820
So when I got where I could,

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.500
that's the story everybody tells, right?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.970
When they get where they can, they do.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:10.803
- Yeah.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:14.400
- But this car has an amazing history.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.480
- Really, what?

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.080
- Well, I owned it for a while

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.130
and then I was gonna put it in the shop.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:22.870
15 minutes after it went
in the shop on a Sunday,

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.286
it was stolen.

00:02:24.286 --> 00:02:25.400
- What?
- Gone.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.710
They crashed through the doors, took it.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.720
It was gone for one month,
two months, three months.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.580
And so it was gone for 10 months.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.290
- That's the craziest story.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.277
- And then finally the
Burbank Police called and said

00:02:39.277 --> 00:02:41.530
"We think we found your car."

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:46.530
And they arrested the King pin
of this mafia group in town

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.010
and an hour and a half later,

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.070
his lawyer pulled up in
front of the police station

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.480
with this on a trailer.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.850
- This is a movie!

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.120
- And it was trashed.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.020
They tried to pick it up with a forklift,

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.410
knock holes in the side,

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.870
they crushed the fins.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.350
But the insurance company paid
for it and got it back to me.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.340
So, it was gone for 10 months.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.050
Now Robin's afraid to ride in it

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.870
'cause she thinks the
mafia is gonna retaliate.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.220
That we wanted the car back.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.120
- You know, that's a
legit concern, Dr. Phil.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.463
- Yeah, I don't know, she's
kinda short, she can duck down.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.800
- Okay, so we're at a drive-in.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.030
Did you grow up doing drive-ins?

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:20.910
- Oh yeah.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:21.743
Everybody talks about

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:23.130
you used to hide your buddy in the truck.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:27.100
- My father made my mother
get in the trunk of a car,

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.790
so he didn't have to pay, you know?

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:29.623
- That was a thing.

00:03:29.623 --> 00:03:34.030
I will say I, have put my
wife in the trunk though.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.080
That's a bad.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.230
- That also sounds like a mafia story.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.150
- Look, I had this Mercedes and it was,

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.420
you remember the old 450 Mercedes?

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.920
The two-seaters?
- Yeah.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.325
- I had one that I loved
and it had a rattle in it.

00:03:47.325 --> 00:03:48.277
- I think I know where this is headed.

00:03:48.277 --> 00:03:49.520
- And I asked Robin.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.820
I said, "Okay, look, do me a favor.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.740
Will you get in the trunk?

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.970
And I'm just gonna drive
around the cul-de-sac

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:59.260
and listen and see if you can
hear where the rattle is."

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.630
And she said, "Get in the trunk?"

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:02.463
I said, "Yeah.

00:04:02.463 --> 00:04:04.133
Listen, I'll put something
down you can get in it."

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:05.430
She said, "Oh, God."

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.967
So she gets in the trunk,

00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:09.270
and I said, "Just kinda hold the lid,

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.630
so you can hear where the rattle is."

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.680
And as we pulled out, I didn't know.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.230
I hit a little bit of a
bump and the trunk latched.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.640
So now she's locked in the trunk.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:20.550
- Oh my God.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.980
- So I pull back in

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.200
and I walked back there
and the trunk is latched.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.940
And it's just one of those
that you push the button.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:27.330
I popped the trunk open.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.347
I said, "Did you hear anything?"

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.560
Oh, did I hear something!
- Oh my God.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.357
- She came climbing out of there.

00:04:35.357 --> 00:04:36.700
- I would have whopped your behind.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.510
- I can't tell you on
daytime television what

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.510
sweet Robin had to say.
(laughter)

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:45.110
You got a rattle in your head,
let me tell you something.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.563
Oh my God, it went from bad to worse.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.248
- All right, well wait.

00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:51.742
- She never found the rattle.

00:04:51.742 --> 00:04:53.312
(laughter)

00:04:53.312 --> 00:04:55.710
(rock music)

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.980
- Okay, I have a question.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.200
Do you think that it's
unhealthy, you know,

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.090
emotionally, mentally to be competitive

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:06.860
with cars and like, you
know, like you wouldn't

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.413
